<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In G.3 Theorem C.2 ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Analysis ‣ Language Modeling with Learned Meta-Tokens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">(i) <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In G.3 Theorem C.2 ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Analysis ‣ Language Modeling with Learned Meta-Tokens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">(ii) There exists a bias <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
