</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 4.1</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\dots,\ell_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\dots,\ell_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be logits and define softmax distribution <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}=\frac{\exp(\ell_{j})}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\exp(\ell_{k})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}=\frac{\exp(\ell_{j})}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\exp(\ell_{k})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that for some "correct" index <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j^{*}}=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j^{*}}=L</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all other indices <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}\leq L-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}\leq L-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, entropy <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing in <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we can group the other logits (i.e. <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum\limits_{j\neq j^{*}}e^{\ell_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum\limits_{j\neq j^{*}}e^{\ell_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, since each <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> carries the property that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\ell_{j}}\leq e^{L-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\ell_{j}}\leq e^{L-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j^{*}}=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j^{*}}=L</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leq(N-1)e^{L-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leq(N-1)e^{L-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> since there are <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> terms. Revisiting the softmax <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j^{*}}=\frac{e^{L}}{e^{L}+S}\geq\frac{e^{L}}{e^{L}+(N-1)e^{L-\Delta}}=\frac{1}{1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j^{*}}=\frac{e^{L}}{e^{L}+S}\geq\frac{e^{L}}{e^{L}+(N-1)e^{L-\Delta}}=\frac{1}{1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will denote this quantity as <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> henceforth. Next, each other softmax <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> must have the property that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}=\frac{e^{\ell}}{e^{L}+S}\leq\frac{e^{L-\Delta}}{e^{L}(1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta})}=\frac{e^{-\Delta}}{1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}=\frac{1-p}{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}=\frac{e^{\ell}}{e^{L}+S}\leq\frac{e^{L-\Delta}}{e^{L}(1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta})}=\frac{e^{-\Delta}}{1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}=\frac{1-p}{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">As a result, we have the following entropy maximization problem:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underset{\alpha_{1},\dots,\alpha_{N}}{\text{maximize}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>maximize</mtext><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msub></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underset{\alpha_{1},\dots,\alpha_{N}}{\text{maximize}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17X.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}\,\log\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}\,\log\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{subject to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>subject to</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{subject to}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17Xa.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex17Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{j^{*}}=p," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{j^{*}}=p,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex17Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex17Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{j}\geq 0,\quad j=1,\dots,N." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{j}\geq 0,\quad j=1,\dots,N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that the entropy (objective) function is Schur-concave in <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, so it is maximized when <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j^{*}}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j^{*}}=p</annotation></semantics></math> and the remaining softmax mass is split uniformly over the <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> elements, i.e. <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}=\frac{1-p}{N-1}\hskip 1.42262pt\forall\hskip 1.42262ptj\neq j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.307em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.307em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}=\frac{1-p}{N-1}\hskip 1.42262pt\forall\hskip 1.42262ptj\neq j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging this in for <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\alpha)\leq-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)+(1-p)\log(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\alpha)\leq-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)+(1-p)\log(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we aim to study the relationship between <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. By the chain rule, <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\Delta}=\frac{dH}{dp}\cdot\frac{dp}{d\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\Delta}=\frac{dH}{dp}\cdot\frac{dp}{d\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{dp}=-(1+\log p)+\log\frac{1-p}{N-1}+1=\log\frac{1-p}{(N-1)p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{dp}=-(1+\log p)+\log\frac{1-p}{N-1}+1=\log\frac{1-p}{(N-1)p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-p}{p}=(N-1)e^{-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-p}{p}=(N-1)e^{-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{dp}=-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{dp}=-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and since <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{dp}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{dp}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We then turn to <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dp}{d\Delta}=\frac{(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}{[1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}]^{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dp}{d\Delta}=\frac{(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}{[1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}]^{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> since both numerator and denominator must be <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\Delta}=-\Delta\frac{(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}{[1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}]^{2}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\Delta}=-\Delta\frac{(N-1)e^{-\Delta}}{[1+(N-1)e^{-\Delta}]^{2}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning that <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing in the margin <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We will now use Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1. ‣ G.1 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Analysis ‣ Language Modeling with Learned Meta-Tokens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> to prove Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.4 Examination of Positional Encoding through Internal Representations. ‣ 4 Results ‣ Language Modeling with Learned Meta-Tokens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem 4.1.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a parametrized path by variable <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,\Delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,\Delta]</annotation></semantics></math>; define <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}^{(t)}=\ell_{j}+\delta_{j,j^{*}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}^{(t)}=\ell_{j}+\delta_{j,j^{*}}t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}^{(t)}=\frac{e^{\ell_{j}^{(t)}}}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}e^{\ell_{k}^{(t)}}}=\frac{e^{(\ell_{j}+\delta_{j,j^{*}}t)}}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}e^{(\ell_{k}+\delta_{k,j^{*}}t)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}^{(t)}=\frac{e^{\ell_{j}^{(t)}}}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}e^{\ell_{k}^{(t)}}}=\frac{e^{(\ell_{j}+\delta_{j,j^{*}}t)}}{\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}e^{(\ell_{k}+\delta_{k,j^{*}}t)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell_{j}^{{}^{\prime}(t)}=\frac{d}{dt}\ell_{j}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}^{{}^{\prime}(t)}=\frac{d}{dt}\ell_{j}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{j}^{{}^{\prime}(t)}=\frac{d}{dt}\alpha_{j}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}^{{}^{\prime}(t)}=\frac{d}{dt}\alpha_{j}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we differentiate the entropy <math id="A7.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A7.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}[\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}+\alpha_{j}\frac{\alpha_{j}^{\prime}}{\alpha_{j}}]=-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}(1+\ln\alpha_{j})=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}+\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}[\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}+\alpha_{j}\frac{\alpha_{j}^{\prime}}{\alpha_{j}}]=-\sum\limits_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}(1+\ln\alpha_{j})=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}+\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum{\alpha_{j}^{\prime}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum{\alpha_{j}^{\prime}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> due to <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\alpha_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\alpha_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, this simply reduces to <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover and Thomas (2006)</a></cite>, we have that <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}^{\prime}=\alpha_{j}(\ell_{j}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}^{\prime}=\alpha_{j}(\ell_{j}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}])</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}\alpha_{k}\ell_{k}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{N}\alpha_{k}\ell_{k}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging this into the expression for the derivative of entropy with respect to <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}(\ell_{j}^{\prime}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]})\ln\alpha_{j}=-(\sum_{j}a_{j}\ell_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]}\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}\ln\alpha_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}(\ell_{j}^{\prime}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]})\ln\alpha_{j}=-(\sum_{j}a_{j}\ell_{j}^{\prime}\ln\alpha_{j}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}[\ell^{\prime}]}\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}\ln\alpha_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that <math id="A7.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}\ln\alpha_{j}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\alpha_{j}\ln\alpha_{j}=\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]</annotation></semantics></math> so this simply reduces as:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-(\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}\ln\alpha]-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}]\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])=-\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-(\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}\ln\alpha]-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}]\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])=-\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Revisiting the meta-token setup where only the "correct" logit at <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is boosted, this suggests that <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}^{\prime}=\textbf{1}(j=j^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">1</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}^{\prime}=\textbf{1}(j=j^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}]=\alpha_{j^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}]=\alpha_{j^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}\ln\alpha]=\alpha_{j^{*}}\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ell^{\prime}\ln\alpha]=\alpha_{j^{*}}\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be substituted into the covariance term above:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)=-(\alpha_{j^{*}}\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\alpha_{j^{*}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])=-\alpha_{j^{*}}(\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)=-\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)=-(\alpha_{j^{*}}\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\alpha_{j^{*}}\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])=-\alpha_{j^{*}}(\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Due to the Schur-concavity of <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marshall et al., 2011</a>)</cite>, <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}=\max_{j}\ln\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}=\max_{j}\ln\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}&gt;\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}&gt;\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, given <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j^{*}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j^{*}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln\alpha_{j^{*}}-\mathop{\mathbb{E}_{\alpha}}[\ln\alpha]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, this suggests that <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}_{\alpha}(\ell^{\prime},\ln\alpha)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus, <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}H(\alpha)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we conclude that adding a positive logit boost at the meta-token index ("correct" logit) strictly decreases entropy, supporting the proposed "anchoring" effect notion.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 5.1</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem 5.1.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The meta-tokens are simply a new (latent) channel that may be utilized to search for candidate distributions. However, this latent can be ignored, yielding the original search space; that is, any encoder <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\hat{x}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\hat{x}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> that does not use meta-tokens can be implemented in the meta-token model by zeroing out all meta-token contributions. Therefore, <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\rm abs}\subseteq\mathcal{Q}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\rm abs}\subseteq\mathcal{Q}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=(q_{\phi},q_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=(q_{\phi},q_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> over the feasible combinations of encoder and decoder. Naturally, minimizing a function over a larger feasible set cannot increase its minimum. Thus, for a fixed rate <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\rm meta}(R)=\min_{q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\rm meta}\,\colon\,I(X;\hat{X})=R}D(q)\;\leq\;\min_{q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\rm abs}\,\colon\,I(X;\hat{X})=R}D(q)=D_{\rm abs}(R)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\rm meta}(R)=\min_{q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\rm meta}\,\colon\,I(X;\hat{X})=R}D(q)\;\leq\;\min_{q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\rm abs}\,\colon\,I(X;\hat{X})=R}D(q)=D_{\rm abs}(R).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the same result holds for RoPE in place of APE (i.e. <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{RoPE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>RoPE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{RoPE}}</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{abs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>abs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{abs}}</annotation></semantics></math>), as well.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Theorem C.2</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem G.2</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider functions <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:\{0,\dots,T-1\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:\{0,\dots,T-1\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:\{-(T-1),\dots,T-1\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:\{-(T-1),\dots,T-1\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for absolute postional biases and relative biases, respectively. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\text{abs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">abs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\text{abs}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the set of all fixed absolute positional bias matrices <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i,j}^{\text{abs}}=p(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">abs</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i,j}^{\text{abs}}=p(j)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\text{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">rel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\text{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the set of all fixed relative biases <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i,j}^{\text{rel}}=b(i-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">rel</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i,j}^{\text{rel}}=b(i-j)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\text{meta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">meta</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\text{meta}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of bias matrices implementable by the Transformer augmented with meta-token embeddings <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{m_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{m_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> which emit a content-dependent logit boost at their respective indices. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{B}_{\text{abs}}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\text{rel}}\subsetneq\mathcal{B}_{\text{meta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">abs</mtext></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">rel</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">meta</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{B}_{\text{abs}}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\text{rel}}\subsetneq\mathcal{B}_{\text{meta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We break this argument down into two parts <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> (i.) the forward direction, where we show that all absolute and relative biases without meta-tokens can be modeled by the meta-token model.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(i) <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by choosing meta-token embeddings <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> at each position <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and a linear head <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the total bias at <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i,j}=\sum_{t}\;Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{t}\;\mathbf{1}_{j=t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i,j}=\sum_{t}\;Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{t}\;\mathbf{1}_{j=t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Absolute case.</em> Given <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(j)</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and choose each <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{j}=p(j)\hskip 2.84526pt\forall\hskip 2.84526pti." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{j}=p(j)\hskip 2.84526pt\forall\hskip 2.84526pti.</annotation></semantics></math>
All other <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t\neq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t\neq j}</annotation></semantics></math> are zero. Then <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i,j}=p(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i,j}=p(j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Relative case.</em> Given <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(i-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(i-j)</annotation></semantics></math>, place a meta-token at every position <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and embeddings <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{j}=b(i-j)\hskip 2.84526pt\forall\hskip 2.84526pti,j." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}^{\top}W\,e_{j}=b(i-j)\hskip 2.84526pt\forall\hskip 2.84526pti,j.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For instance, if we let <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\mathrm{I}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\mathrm{I}d</annotation></semantics></math> and arrange that <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the vector <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(b(1-j),b(2-j),\dots,b(T-j)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(b(1-j),b(2-j),\dots,b(T-j)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}^{\top}e_{j}=b(i-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}^{\top}e_{j}=b(i-j)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.I1.i2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th standard basis vector.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, every absolute or relative bias (in <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}</annotation></semantics></math>) lies in <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(ii) There exists a bias <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define a content-dependent bias
<math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}_{i,j}=f\bigl(C_{j}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}_{i,j}=f\bigl(C_{j}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the full token context preceding position <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is any non-constant function. Such a <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> arises by setting each meta-token embedding <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}=f(C_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}=f(C_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\mathrm{I}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\mathrm{I}d</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, if there was <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(j)=f(C_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(j)=f(C_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and all possible <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is impossible since <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> varies. Furthermore, if <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\in\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(i-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(i-j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(i-j)=f(C_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(i-j)=f(C_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>; again, this condition is impossible to be satisfied. Therefore <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>abs</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}\notin\mathcal{B}_{\rm abs}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\rm rel}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As a result, we conclude that the biases represented by <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\rm meta}</annotation></semantics></math> contain the set of both absolute and relative biases without meta-tokens, and represent additional biases that cannot be represented without meta-tokens.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The result of Theorem <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem G.2. ‣ G.3 Theorem C.2 ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Analysis ‣ Language Modeling with Learned Meta-Tokens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a> is that the introduction of meta-tokens strictly grows the expressivity of biases that may be represented, while still being entirely inclusive of the fixed realizable absolute and relative encoding biases. As a result, we do not "lose" anything representationally by introducing meta-tokens, from a positional biases standpoint. This enhanced expressive power also plays a role in enabling the model to learn to focus attention on relevant context spans, reinforcing the aforementioned sharpening effect.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Example Prompts for Synthetic Tasks</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide example prompts and target completions for each synthetic task used in our experiments. Each example illustrates the input format, the placement of <span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">_PAUSE_</span> meta-tokens, and the expected model output.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">List Recall</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
Fruits: orange peach banana plum
Tools: hammer wrench level pliers
Sports: boxing baseball boxing golf
Spices: turmeric cardamom cumin cinnamon
Animals: cat tiger wolf fox
Professions: teacher nurse lawyer architect
Vegetables: onion cucumber broccoli cucumber
Instruments: piano clarinet violin piano
Professions: teacher nurse lawyer _PAUSE_ architect
Q: What is item 3 of Professions? _PAUSE_
</pre>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
lawyer
</pre>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Segment Counting</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
Fruits: orange peach banana plum
Tools: _PAUSE_ hammer wrench level pliers _PAUSE_
Sports: boxing baseball boxing golf
Spices: turmeric cardamom cumin cinnamon
Q: How many times does wrench appear between the pauses around Tools? _PAUSE_
</pre>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
1
</pre>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parity</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
Bits: 0 _PAUSE_ 1 0 0
Q: What is the XOR of all bits before this pause? _PAUSE_
</pre>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
0
</pre>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Copying</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
...as ever Mr _PAUSE_ . Darcy had been, was much
relieved by discerning such different feelings.

They had not been long together before Darcy told her that Bingley was
also coming to wait on her; and she had barely time to express her
satisfaction, and prepare for such a visitor, when Bingley’s quick step
was heard on the stairs, and in a moment he entered the room. All
Elizabeth’s anger against him had been long done away; but had she still
felt any, it could hardly have stood its ground against the unaffected
cordiality with which he expressed himself on seeing her again. He
inquired in a friendly, though general, way, after her family, and
looked and spoke with the same _PAUSE_ good-humoured ease that he had ever done.
Q: Copy the bracketed text. _PAUSE_
</pre>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion:</span></p><pre id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
. Darcy had been, was much
relieved by discerning such different feelings.

They had not been long together before Darcy told her that Bingley was
also coming to wait on her; and she had barely time to express her
satisfaction, and prepare for such a visitor, when Bingley’s quick step
was heard on the stairs, and in a moment he entered the room. All
Elizabeth’s anger against him had been long done away; but had she still
felt any, it could hardly have stood its ground against the unaffected
cordiality with which he expressed himself on seeing her again. He
inquired in a friendly, though general, way, after her family, and
looked and spoke with the same.
</pre>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Broader Impacts Statement</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work on learned meta-tokens and meta-attention offers a lightweight, data-efficient way to pre-train language models while demonstrating strong performance when fine-tuned for recall tasks. This suggests a path toward more capable, leaner language models that could be used to handle contexts such as like long legal or medical documents, extended multi-turn dialogues, or large codebases without resorting to prohibitively large architectures or expensive fine-tuning runs. Such models could bring real benefits to areas such as conversational agents for education or healthcare. Building off of prior literature that performs a more explicit learned retrieval from the context <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mohtashami and Jaggi, 2023</a>)</cite>, this could induce improved and efficient in-line retrieval over vast corpora.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our work relates strongly to the recent debates in the language modeling community on the impact of positional encoding, particularly around works such as NoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kazemnejad et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. We provide strong evidence that zeroing the positional encoding can improve performance, providing motivation for hybrid attention mechanisms such as RNoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and other, more efficient ways to pre-train language models with long-context modeling settings in mind. We note that advances in long-context modeling could introduce risks around misuse and unintended harm. More powerful context understanding over long ranges can fuel phishing text and distracted models, especially in the phase of noisy context. However, models trained on corpora without data pre-processing a priori may be subject to harmful behavior such as profane generations. In the context of our work, which uses standard, pre-filtered corpora, this issue is avoided; we encourage users to audit the data used for pre-training first.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
